If `content` is `"secret\0data"`, `strlen(content)` is 6.
`content[strlen(content) + 1]` would be `content[7]`, which is 'd'.
So `content[strlen(content) + 1] != '\0'` would be true, and it would return. This is correct.
This approach correctly identifies and rejects strings with embedded null bytes.
